    "forecast": "low",
    "rationale": "Reviewed prompt, tool manifest, and runtime notes only. The design is narrowly scoped: one trusted user input channel, one read-only internal search capability, and one reply channel bound to the authenticated requester. Structural controls sever the main risk paths: least-privilege read-only access to the policy index, reply binding to the authenticated session, and verified network egress denial. No present finding exceeds low, and considered forecast triggers do not raise the tier unless the design materially changes and should be reassessed."
